```python
import math

def shout(text):
    return text.upper()


def first_index(items, target):
    for i in range(1, len(items)):
        if items[i] == target:
            return i
    return -1
```

The bug is in the `first_index` function. It starts searching from index `1`, which means it will skip the first element at index `0`. If the target is in the first position, it will incorrectly return `-1`.

